//? Title: Spectral GAN: Cached Directions, Live Weight Gradients
//? Subtitle: Explicit power iteration, state–D–G writes and measured normalization error
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A compact GAN fits 1000 balanced MNIST images with two spectrally normalized discriminator
kernels. Cached left/right directions are checkpointed separately from trainable weights:
sixteen warm-up power iterations precede the initial snapshot, and one state-only iteration
precedes every discriminator update. The generator then fits through the updated discriminator
with the same cached vectors. The signed bilinear denominator remains differentiable in the
weights, while the vectors are held constant in backpropagation. Three fixed epochs perform
96 writes per trainable store and produce weak grey samples. The complete editable native
program preserves every original artifact; small matrix examples, independent derivatives
and an SVD audit explain why estimated normalization is not an exact unit-norm certificate.
)
\toc

> Follow data, weights and cached directions

The method reference is [Miyato et al., Spectral Normalization for Generative Adversarial
Networks (2018)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957). This repository retains its own small
teaching architecture: G maps16 Gaussian coordinates through32 tanh units to784 sigmoid
pixels; image-only D maps784 pixels through32 tanh units to one raw score. Both D kernels
are normalized; their biases are untouched. Digit labels do not enter fitting. The dense
architecture, Float32 guards and state schedule below specify this example rather than
reproducing the paper's convolutional benchmarks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spectral_gan_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(52, 1250);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;
  s.width     = 7.5;
  s.height    = 3.;
  s.font_size = 26;
  d.node("real", {-15, 9}, "Real pixels784", s)
      .node("dr", {15, 9}, "Shared spectral D\nRaw source score", s)
      .node("noise", {-15, 0}, "Gaussian noise16", s)
      .node("g", {-5, 0}, "Independent G\ntanh32 → sigmoid784", s)
      .node("fake", {5, 0}, "Generated pixels784", s)
      .node("df", {15, 0}, "Same D kernels\nSame cached u/v", s)
      .node("weights", {-15, -9}, "Current D weights\nheld fixed in Advance", s)
      .node("advance", {-5, -9}, "Explicit power step\nv=unit(Wu); u=unit(Wᵀv)", s)
      .node("cache", {5, -9}, "Separate u/v state\nStopped in backprop", s)
      .edge("real", "dr")
      .edge("noise", "g")
      .edge("g", "fake")
      .edge("fake", "df")
      .edge("weights", "advance")
      .edge("advance", "cache")
      .edge("cache", "df")
      .text(
          {0, -14}, "Per batch: advance state → write D → fresh forward, same cache → write G", 19)
      .save_svg("build/spectral_gan_method.svg");
}
```
