> Check one normalized matrix and its weight derivative

For W=diag(3,2) and cached columns u=v=(1,0)ᵀ, sigma=vᵀWu=3 and
Wbar=diag(1,2/3). Holding u/v fixed does not make sigma constant in W.
For L=sum(Wbar), the derivative at W00 is 1/3−5/9=−2/9; the other three
entries are1/3. Detaching sigma would incorrectly give1/3 for every entry.
The example checks the live denominator derivative and a scalar finite difference.

Power iteration instead starts from u=(1,1)ᵀ/sqrt(2). Each iteration sets
v=Wu/sqrt(sum((Wu)²)+epsilon), then u=Wᵀv/sqrt(sum((Wᵀv)²)+epsilon).
There is no extra initial normalization. The plot measures the effective matrix's
SVD norm after each iteration; a finite approximation may leave it above one.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spectral_gan_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto t      = n::DType::Float64;
  auto w      = n::tensor({3., 0., 0., 2.}, {2, 2}, t).requires_grad_(),
       u = n::tensor({1., 0.}, {2, 1}, t), v = u;
  auto out        = n::cached_spectral_kernel(w, u, v);
  auto derivative = n::grad(n::sum(out.weight), {w})[0];
  auto expected   = n::tensor({-2. / 9, 1. / 3, 1. / 3, 1. / 3}, {2, 2}, t);
  if (n::max(n::abs(derivative - expected)).item() > 1e-14)
    throw std::runtime_error("live sigma derivative");
  auto plus   = n::tensor({3.000001, 0., 0., 2.}, {2, 2}, t),
       minus  = n::tensor({2.999999, 0., 0., 2.}, {2, 2}, t);
  auto finite = (n::sum(n::cached_spectral_kernel(plus, u, v).weight).item() -
                 n::sum(n::cached_spectral_kernel(minus, u, v).weight).item()) /
                2e-6;
  if (std::abs(finite + 2. / 9) > 1e-9)
    throw std::runtime_error("finite difference");
  std::print(
      "sigma={} ; Wbar diagonal=1,2/3 ; dL/dW00={} ; finite difference={}\n",
      out.sigma.item(),
      derivative.at({0, 0}),
      finite);
  u = n::full({2, 1}, 1 / std::sqrt(2.), t);
  std::vector<double> x, y;
  for (int i = 1; i <= 12; ++i) {
    auto pair = n::cached_spectral_power_iteration(w, u);
    u         = pair.u;
    x.push_back(i);
    y.push_back(n::svd(n::cached_spectral_kernel(w, u, pair.v).weight).s.at({0}));
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(.997, 1.13)
      .lines(x, y, "Measured SVD norm", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .lines({1., 12.}, {1., 1.}, "Unit reference", {120, 120, 120}, 1.)
      .x_label("Completed ordered power iterations")
      .y_label("SVD norm of W / cached sigma")
      .title("Finite iteration approaches the top direction")
      .save_svg("build/spectral_gan_toy.svg");
}
```
