\image(figures/spectral_gan_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The curve uses native tensor power iteration and native SVD on the same2×2 kernel. The analytic derivative includes the changing denominator.)
\alttext(Twelve measured effective-kernel norms approach the horizontal unit reference from above.)

The reusable cache API accepts positive finite Float32/64 CPU kernels of rank at least two,
flattening all leading axes as input. Vectors are columns u[out,1],v[in,1]. It computes
sigma=sum(detach(v)*(flatten(W)*detach(u))) and divides W by max(sigma,floor), without
an absolute value. Default floor is double(1e-6f) and squared-norm epsilon is double(1e-12f),
preserving Float32-rounded guards even for Float64 inputs. Zero kernels yield zero power
vectors; a negative/zero sigma uses the positive floor. First/higher weight paths stay live,
both vector paths stop. Invalid or nonfinite computations are rejected.

`advance_cached_spectral_state` reads all /W kernels and existing matching /u,/v pairs,
computes every next pair, then writes only cache values. Missing or malformed state fails
before any write. Cache leaves follow ParameterStore's requires_grad flags, but the math
always detaches them and no optimizer owns them. Checkpoint all three stores and synchronize
shared-store mutations. `SpectralGan` never advances existing state implicitly.

> Start with source scores whose losses can be checked by hand

For separate real and fake pools,

\[L_D=\operatorname{mean}\max(0,1-r)+\operatorname{mean}\max(0,1+f),\quad L_G=-\operatorname{mean}f.\]

The real branch stops contributing to D at r≥1; the fake branch stops at f≤-1.
At exactly r=1 or f=-1, native ReLU uses the zero subgradient. G has no hinge:
its derivative remains -1/M everywhere, including those margins. G loss can be
negative, and D scores need not lie in[-1,1]. At scalar r=1,f=-1, D=0,G=1 and
D's two derivatives are zero while G's fake-score derivative is-1. Zero-margin
D gradients do not imply convergence of image generation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spectral_gan_derivatives.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::vector<double> x, dr, df, gf;
  for (int k = -60; k <= 60; ++k) {
    x.push_back(k / 20.);
    auto r          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
         f          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
    const auto loss = n::models::HingeGanObjectives(r, f);
    const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
    dr.push_back(d[0].item());
    df.push_back(d[1].item());
    gf.push_back(n::grad(n::models::HingeGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f})[0].item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, dr, "D real derivative", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines(x, df, "D fake derivative", {22, 163, 74}, 2.)
      .lines(x, gf, "G fake derivative", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .y_limits(-1.5, 2)
      .x_label("Respective scalar raw source score")
      .y_label("Derivative; each pool size1")
      .title("Hinge objective: distinguish D and G directions")
      .save_svg("build/spectral_gan_derivatives.svg");
  auto r          = n::full({1, 1}, 1., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
       f          = n::full({1, 1}, -1., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
  const auto loss = n::models::HingeGanObjectives(r, f);
  const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
  const auto g    = n::grad(n::models::HingeGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f});
  std::print(
      "Hand-check: D={:.9f},G={:.9f}; D derivatives={},{}; G derivative={}.\n",
      loss.discriminator.item(),
      loss.generator.item(),
      d[0].item(),
      d[1].item(),
      g[0].item());
}
```
