> Native preparation and separated digit pools

The program prepares the native `mnist-assets` recipe and loads its saliency pools.
Fitting/validation are disjoint subsets of original MNIST training data; test IDs remain
in the original test range. Every class contributes 100 fitting and 20 validation/test
images. The loader checks shape, IDs, balance and pixel scaling to Float32[0,1].
The preview takes the first two fitting observations per class, without model selection.
Labels describe the dataset balance and preview only; fitting ignores them.
The initial test forward is archived as an explicit diagnostic control; test outcomes never
choose weights, noise banks, hyperparameters or epochs. Validation only logs diagnostics.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spectral_gan_pools.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto home   = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home());
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", home);
  auto                      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(home / "saliency");
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  auto                      labels = pools[0].labels.to_vector<std::int32_t>();
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    int count = 0;
    for (std::int64_t k = 0; k < 1000 && count < 2; ++k)
      if (labels[k] == c) {
        rows.push_back(k);
        ++count;
      }
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), "build/spectral_gan_pools.png", 2, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
  std::print(
      "| pool | rows | each class | role |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| fitting |1000|100| Adam updates "
      "|\n| validation |200|20| log only |\n| test |200|20| fixed final evaluation |\n");
}
```
