> Audit the final cached estimate with an SVD

The source audit promotes final W,u,v to Float64, recomputes sigma in Float64, divides
by max(sigma,1e-6), and takes the largest singular value. This is an audit of a Float64
recomputation from the saved Float32 checkpoint, not an SVD of a previously rounded
Float32 Wbar. The hidden norm is about1.008681 and output1.000000028. Finite power
iteration and weight movement after the state step leave a measurable approximation
error. These values are reported without a unit-kernel or whole-network certificate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spectral_gan_norms.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/spectral_gan/final.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  std::vector<double> norms;
  std::print("| kernel | Float64 audit SVD norm |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string name : {"hidden", "output"}) {
    auto w     = n::cast(a.at("1/" + name + "/W"), n::DType::Float64),
         u     = n::cast(a.at("2/" + name + "/u"), n::DType::Float64),
         v     = n::cast(a.at("2/" + name + "/v"), n::DType::Float64);
    auto sigma = n::sum(v * n::matmul(w, u));
    auto norm  = n::svd(w / std::max(sigma.item(), 1e-6)).s.at({0});
    norms.push_back(norm);
    std::print("| {} | {:.12f} |\n", name, norm);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(.998, 1.016)
      .lines({.5, 2.5}, {1., 1.}, "Unit reference", {120, 120, 120}, 1.)
      .points({1.}, {norms[0]}, "Hidden784×32", {37, 99, 235}, 5.)
      .points({2.}, {norms[1]}, "Output32×1", {220, 38, 38}, 5.)
      .x_label("Kernel: hidden at1; output at2")
      .y_label("SVD norm after Float64 recomputation")
      .title("Final cached normalization retains approximation error")
      .save_svg("build/spectral_gan_norms.svg");
}
```
